# For more information on these fields, see:
# https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/adding_to_third_party.md#readme_chromium
#
# TaffyGo vendors the EasyList family under //taffy rather than under
# Chromium's own //third_party because which rule sets the product blocks with
# is a TaffyGo product decision, not an upstream one: decision 0076 records the
# choice and OD-070's resolution. Unlike the flag-icons recipe next door, the
# upstream snapshots ARE committed here: easylist.to serves only the current
# list, so a digest pin with no bytes behind it would stop being reproducible
# the day upstream rolls, and the tree is the only durable place to keep the
# exact bytes the pack was built from.

Name: easylist
Short Name: easylist
URL: https://easylist.to/easylist/easylist.txt
Version: 202608272347
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: GPL-3.0
License File: vendor/easylist.GPL3.txt
Shipped: yes
Security Critical: no

Description:
The base ad and tracker rule sets the filtering plane blocks with: EasyList
202608272347 and EasyPrivacy 202608272349, taken from easylist.to as pinned
snapshots. Built by tools/build_filter_pack.py into one deterministic zip of
the two lists plus their licence, catalogued for the delivery plane as asset
`easylist-base`. The snapshots and the recipe live here.

Shipped is "yes" because the APK carries the lists twice (decision 0202).
`:bundled_filter_list_assets` in this directory's BUILD.gn packages the two
snapshots, concatenated, as `taffy-filter-lists/base.txt`, and
//taffy/components/delivery:bundled_delivery_assets packages the
`easylist-base` zip, which is seeded into the delivery store on first run.
Nothing fetches them from a host. Decision 0206 needs this field to be true:
the credits page is generated from it, and a part recorded as not shipped is
left out of the notice the package carries.

Both lists are dual-licensed GPL-3.0 / CC BY-SA 3.0 by the EasyList authors
(https://easylist.to/pages/licence.html). This vendoring elects GPL-3.0, and
the licence text travels inside the pack as its own LICENSE member so a device
that has the rules has the terms beside them. The lists are data the browser
reads, not code it links: nothing derived from them enters this repository's
own source.

Local Modifications:
None. The snapshots are byte-for-byte what easylist.to served on
2026-08-27 (UTC); the pack carries them verbatim under lists/ beside the
licence.
